/compare/0.5.1-ls13...0.5.2-ls14","upstream":"# SealSkin 0.5.2\n\nMaintenance release.\n\n## Collaboration\n\n* **Collaboration profiles.** An administrator assigns a profile to users\n  and groups under **Collaboration profile**, and it decides what their\n  collaboration rooms may do. Chat, cameras, microphones, the application\n  switcher, mouse and keyboard handoff, gamepads, collaborator invites, and\n  viewer invites can each be turned off, and collaborators can be kept from\n  sharing viewer invites. A profile can also keep the stream at the\n  controller's resolution and cap how many people may join a room. The\n  server refuses whatever a profile turns off, whatever a guest's page\n  sends. Where a user's groups name several profiles, each feature takes the\n  most restrictive. A room keeps the rules it started under. The form\n  previews the room's bar as the controller, a collaborator, and a viewer see\n  it. Profiles are kept in the shared record `collaboration_profiles.yml`\n  (`SEALSKIN_COLLABORATION_PROFILES_PATH`). A user under no profile gets\n  every feature, as before.\n* **People in a room.** The room's bar has a people button that lists\n  everyone in the room, viewers included, with whether their microphone and\n  camera are on and what input they hold. The controller can hand a\n  collaborator the mouse and keyboard from it. Bugfix: A participant whose \n  camera is off keeps a tile.\n\n## Fixes\n\n* With `SEALSKIN_AUTO_SIGN_IN=oidc`, an application's address such as\n  `/app/<app_id>/` is now kept through the identity provider's round trip,\n  so the user lands on that application after signing in rather than on the\n  home page.\n","upstream_url":"https://github.com/selkies-project/sealskin/releases/tag/0.5.2"},"config":{"env":["PATH=/lsiopy/bin:/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin","PS1=$(whoami)@$(hostname):$(pwd)\\$ ","HOME=/config","TERM=xterm","S6_CMD_WAIT_FOR_SERVICES_MAXTIME=0","S6_VERBOSITY=1","S6_STAGE2_HOOK=/docker-mods","VIRTUAL_ENV=/lsiopy","LSIO_FIRST_PARTY=true"],"exposed_ports":["8000/tcp","8443/tcp"],"volumes":["/config","/storage"],"entrypoint":["/init"],"working_dir":"/"},"is_newest":true,"links":{"build":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/hub/api/v1/catalog/sealskin/builds/0.5.2-ls14.json","diff":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/hub/api/v1/catalog/sealskin/builds/0.5.2-ls14/diff.json","layers":{"amd64":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/hub/api/v1/catalog/sealskin/builds/0.5.2-ls14/layers.amd64.json","arm64":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/hub/api/v1/catalog/sealskin/builds/0.5.2-ls14/layers.arm64.json"},"packages":{"amd64":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/hub/api/v1/catalog/sealskin/builds/0.5.2-ls14/packages.amd64.json","arm64":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/hub/api/v1/catalog/sealskin/builds/0.5.2-ls14/packages.arm64.json"},"release":"https://github.com/linuxserver-playground/docker-sealskin/releases/tag/0.5.2-ls14","pages":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/docker-sealskin/builds/0.5.2-ls14/","files":{"amd64":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/docker-sealskin/builds/0.5.2-ls14/files.amd64.json.gz","arm64":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/docker-sealskin/builds/0.5.2-ls14/files.arm64.json.gz"},"sbom":{"amd64":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/docker-sealskin/builds/0.5.2-ls14/packages.amd64.json.gz","arm64":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/docker-sealskin/builds/0.5.2-ls14/packages.arm64.json.gz"},"run_json":"https://github.com/linuxserver-playground/docker-sealskin/releases/download/0.5.2-ls14/run.json","logs_zip":"https://github.com/linuxserver-playground/docker-sealskin/releases/download/0.5.2-ls14/logs.zip","test_report":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/site/images/sealskin/builds/0.5.2-ls14/","tests":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/hub/api/v1/catalog/sealskin/builds/0.5.2-ls14/tests.json","report":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/hub